{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-lagrangian","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:categorical-lagrangian","kind":"definition","title":"Categorical Lagrangian","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-dirac-operator"],"tags":["lagrangian","dirac","endomorphism"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalLagrangian","text":"categorical-lagrangian.md","leanSource":"categorical-lagrangian.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:categorical-lagrangian\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe with categorical Dirac operator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{D}_\\nabla</code> and a state <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\psi \\colon \\mathbf{1} \\to A</code>. The <strong>categorical Lagrangian</strong> is the endomorphism</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathcal{L}_q(\\nabla, \\psi)\n  = \n  \\mathcal{D}_\\nabla^{2} +\n  \\psi^* \\otimes \\mathcal{D}_\\nabla\\psi\n   \\in  \\mathrm{End}_{\\mathbf{C}}(A),</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\psi^* = \\int_A \\!\\circ S(\\psi) \\colon A \\to \\mathbf{1}</code> is the adjoint section.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-lagrangian.md","heading":"Definition","number":"4.13.1","page":"b/def-categorical-lagrangian","qa":{"counts":{"pass":80,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":67},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.CategoricalLagrangian","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-lagrangian.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
